        "title": "feat(durable): add durable runtime core",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nBuilds the durable runtime core on top of the canonical durable-runtime RFC/status PR #101828:\n\n- adds the durable runtime model, SQLite store, recovery/fan-in/orchestration primitives, worker surface, and gateway methods\n- wires agent/session runtime effects and context refs needed for durable runs\n- adds guardrails/tests for schema lifecycle, task completion policy, gateway protocol, and embedded-agent retry behavior\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAgent/session work currently has runtime state and lifecycle edges that are difficult to recover, replay, or reason about across process failures. This PR adds the durable runtime core needed to persist task/run state, recover or fan in work safely, expose gateway controls, and keep embedded-agent session effects typed and observable while preserving the canonical PR1 cleanup behavior.\n\n## Stack / base reconciliation\n\n- Canonical PR1/RFC: #101828 (`🦐 gold shrimp`, threshold met)\n- Corrected PR2 branch: `codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-core-v2-pr101828-ready`\n- Corrected local head: `099ffa5dbc` (`fix(durable): type session effects on embedded runs`)\n- Base: `origin/pr/101828` at `98ffd6a2fb`\n- The prior beta2-prepared branch (`codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-core-v2-ready` at `2f6d9e7a96`) was not submitted because comparing it against current `main` or #101828 would have been cumulative/misleading.\n- This corrected branch manually replays the five PR2 commits onto #101828. The replay conflict in `src/gateway/server-methods/agent.ts` was resolved by preserving the canonical PR1 `activeRunAbort.cleanup({ force: true })` cleanup shape while adding durable lifecycle close on undispatched failures.\n\n## Non-cumulative diff check\n\n- `git log --oneline --reverse origin/pr/101828..HEAD` shows exactly five PR2 replay commits:\n  - `c851808aa3 feat(durable): add runtime foundation`\n  - `c31b49c366 feat(durable): wire agent session runtime`\n  - `1bb1edf8cc fix(durable): harden runtime store and controls`\n  - `12a58c5ceb fix(durable): align runtime schema guardrails`\n  - `099ffa5dbc fix(durable): type session effects on embedded runs`\n- `git diff --name-status origin/pr/101828..HEAD` is scoped to durable runtime core, gateway durable methods/protocol wiring, session/runtime effects, schema guardrails, and related tests.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm exec vitest run src/durable/*.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts`\n  - passed, 15 files / 55 tests\n  - artifact: `/tmp/pr2-pr101828-vitest-durable.log`\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`\n  - passed\n  - artifact: `/tmp/pr2-pr101828-tsgo-core.log`\n- GitHub check diagnosis: initial `Real behavior proof` failed only because the external PR body lacked authored `What Problem This Solves` and `Evidence` sections; those sections are now included here.\n",
